### InventorySystem API - example requests
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension, JetBrains Rider/IntelliJ's
### built-in HTTP client, or Visual Studio 2022's built-in .http support.
### Run requests top to bottom - later ones reuse variables captured from
### earlier responses (e.g. {{login.response.body.token}}).
###
### Point @host at whichever way you're running the API:
###   docker compose up          -> http://localhost:8080
###   dotnet run (LocalDB, dev)  -> https://localhost:5443 (or your launchSettings port)

@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Log in as the seeded admin user (see AppDbContextSeed for all three demo accounts)
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### 2. List categories (any authenticated role can read)
GET {{host}}/api/Categories
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 3. List products - paginated, searchable, sortable
GET {{host}}/api/Products?page=1&pageSize=10&sortBy=price_desc
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 4. Create a product
# @name createProduct
POST {{host}}/api/Products
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "DEMO-0001",
  "name": "Demo Widget",
  "unitOfMeasure": "each",
  "unitPrice": 12.50,
  "reorderLevel": 5,
  "categoryId": 1
}

### 5. List warehouses (to find a warehouseId for the next step)
GET {{host}}/api/Warehouses
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 6. Record stock coming IN for the new product
POST {{host}}/api/stock/movements
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": {{createProduct.response.body.id}},
  "warehouseId": 1,
  "type": "In",
  "quantity": 50,
  "reference": "DEMO-RECEIPT-1"
}

### 7. Check the stock level - should show the 50 units just recorded
GET {{host}}/api/stock/levels/product/{{createProduct.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 8. Try to take out more than is on hand - demonstrates the atomic
### "can't go negative" guarantee: this returns 409 Conflict and step 9
### below will show the level is completely unchanged.
POST {{host}}/api/stock/movements
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": {{createProduct.response.body.id}},
  "warehouseId": 1,
  "type": "Out",
  "quantity": 9999
}

### 9. Confirm nothing was written by the rejected request above
GET {{host}}/api/stock/levels/product/{{createProduct.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 10. Transfer stock between warehouses (atomic: one Out leg + one In leg)
POST {{host}}/api/stock/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": {{createProduct.response.body.id}},
  "sourceWarehouseId": 1,
  "destinationWarehouseId": 2,
  "quantity": 10
}

### 11. Low-stock report
GET {{host}}/api/reports/low-stock
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 12. Stock valuation, grouped by warehouse
GET {{host}}/api/reports/stock-valuation?by=warehouse
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 13. Stock valuation, grouped by category
GET {{host}}/api/reports/stock-valuation?by=category
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 14. Movement history for the demo product, paginated
GET {{host}}/api/reports/movement-history?productId={{createProduct.response.body.id}}&page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 15. Create a purchase order
# @name createPO
POST {{host}}/api/PurchaseOrders
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "supplierId": 1,
  "items": [
    { "productId": {{createProduct.response.body.id}}, "quantityOrdered": 20, "unitCost": 8.00 }
  ]
}

### 16. Send the purchase order (Draft -> Sent)
POST {{host}}/api/PurchaseOrders/{{createPO.response.body.id}}/send
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 17. Receive it - this triggers an In stock movement per line item
POST {{host}}/api/PurchaseOrders/{{createPO.response.body.id}}/receive
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "warehouseId": 1,
  "items": [
    { "purchaseOrderItemId": {{createPO.response.body.items[0].id}}, "quantityReceived": 20 }
  ]
}

### 18. Log in as staff (a lower-privileged role) to demonstrate 403 on delete
# @name loginStaff
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "staff",
  "password": "Staff123!"
}

### 19. Staff attempting to delete a product - expect 403 Forbidden
### (Admin or Manager tokens succeed with 204 instead - see role policy in
### ProductsController.)
DELETE {{host}}/api/Products/{{createProduct.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStaff.response.body.token}}

### 20. No token at all - expect 401 Unauthorized
GET {{host}}/api/Products
